WEBVTT

00:02.170 --> 00:04.490
<i>The combat tournament has begun.</i>

00:04.490 --> 00:06.930
<i>In the first round, Daena faces Yuno.</i>

00:07.250 --> 00:13.200
<i>Due to a noble's dastardly scheme, 
my students will be fighting one another.</i>

00:17.770 --> 00:20.240
<i>And yet, they cannot go easy on each other.</i>

00:20.240 --> 00:23.270
<i>Competition is always without mercy.</i>

00:26.080 --> 00:28.170
The winner is Daena Severus.

00:48.150 --> 00:50.030
<b>Season Two</b>

02:01.140 --> 02:05.400
<b>Night Fifteen   A Fierce Tournament</b>

02:01.140 --> 02:05.400
<b>Night Fifteen   A Fierce Tournament</b>

02:01.940 --> 02:04.940
The next match will be the 
tournament's highest-level fight.

02:04.940 --> 02:07.640
Both combatants are level 97.

02:08.120 --> 02:09.840
First, Jin Rohan.

02:11.180 --> 02:13.570
His opponent, Mithra Casper.

02:14.600 --> 02:18.250
In this tournament, a handful of 
participants are over level 90.

02:19.800 --> 02:25.540
In order to keep the playing field even, 
they will be using wooden swords.

02:25.540 --> 02:29.740
<i>Yeah, right. They're just 
doing it to spite my students.</i>

02:30.090 --> 02:32.130
The match will last ten minutes.

02:32.130 --> 02:37.050
For safety reasons, those dolls will 
incur any damage taken by the students.

02:37.050 --> 02:39.100
Those are the dolls?

02:39.100 --> 02:39.760
Yeah.

02:40.050 --> 02:46.060
The students don't take damage, but if 
even a single doll falls, the match is over.

02:46.490 --> 02:50.510
Each student is given three 
dolls in case of overkills.

02:51.480 --> 02:53.860
Three wouldn't be enough.

02:56.390 --> 03:00.530
Only self-supporting spells can 
be used in the warrior category.

03:01.420 --> 03:04.450
Attack and healing spells are prohibited.

03:05.160 --> 03:06.250
Now, then...

03:08.330 --> 03:09.780
Begin!

03:11.490 --> 03:12.850
Let's make this quick.

03:12.850 --> 03:13.700
No hard feelings.

03:14.650 --> 03:16.640
Sure. Don't hold back.

03:18.340 --> 03:19.900
What's wrong with you, big guy?

03:19.900 --> 03:20.990
You're just defending!

03:20.990 --> 03:22.290
Attack him!

03:22.540 --> 03:26.300
Mithra's defensive movements 
and positioning are better.

03:26.650 --> 03:29.390
He's effectively dampening 
his opponent's spirit.

03:29.390 --> 03:34.020
Yeah. The only reason his opponent hasn't 
stopped attacking is because he's Jin.

03:35.870 --> 03:38.650
If this match were determined by 
judgment, Jin would be the winner.

03:44.650 --> 03:46.670
The winner is Jin Rohan.

03:48.630 --> 03:50.930
Your students didn't disappoint.

03:50.930 --> 03:53.400
That was a rather high-level match.

03:53.400 --> 03:56.540
Personally, I believe Mithra won that fight.

03:56.540 --> 03:59.870
You mean he won the fight 
but lost the match?

04:00.130 --> 04:04.510
I know exactly what Jin is thinking.

04:05.940 --> 04:06.850
Begin!

04:07.480 --> 04:10.140
O spirits, hear my prayer.

04:07.480 --> 04:10.320
O goddess, grant me your strength.

04:10.140 --> 04:14.060
Grant me swift arrows of ice, so that I may...

04:10.320 --> 04:12.730
Grant me the red miracle of destruction.

04:12.730 --> 04:14.060
Form your flames into a spear...

04:16.890 --> 04:19.740
The mage category is a mess.

04:19.740 --> 04:22.750
All the students except yours 
are doing a sloppy job.

04:22.750 --> 04:25.580
Even orc children are better than this.

04:27.180 --> 04:30.180
They seem to be taking it seriously, though.

04:30.210 --> 04:31.370
Go!

04:30.620 --> 04:33.310
The audience around us seems delighted, too.

04:31.370 --> 04:32.280
That's it!

04:32.280 --> 04:33.040
Amazing!

04:33.040 --> 04:34.360
More!

04:34.360 --> 04:35.060
Yeah...

04:36.870 --> 04:39.050
<i>Next is Abelia and Shifu's match.</i>

04:39.820 --> 04:43.400
<i>Before summer break, 
their levels were even, but...</i>

04:45.130 --> 04:46.470
Az kafra swen!

04:47.080 --> 04:47.920
She's charging in?

04:47.920 --> 04:49.130
Isn't she a mage?

04:49.430 --> 04:51.840
Flaga ankasha mavis staja!

04:52.200 --> 04:55.900
<i>She's quick. She completed the 
incantation while evading her attack.</i>

04:58.310 --> 05:02.100
She moved like she was expecting 
that arrow to follow her.

05:03.240 --> 05:04.360
Crap—

05:05.430 --> 05:08.570
But her opponent expected her to evade it.

05:10.980 --> 05:13.360
Spirits of the earth, seize my enemy.

05:17.120 --> 05:18.030
What is that?

05:18.030 --> 05:20.100
I've never seen that spell before!

05:20.100 --> 05:22.080
An earth spirit spell, huh?

05:29.280 --> 05:30.860
I surrender.

05:31.220 --> 05:33.700
The winner is Shifu Rembrandt.

05:34.800 --> 05:37.770
I wonder, how would they fare in a real fight?

05:38.400 --> 05:42.210
<i>The way this is going, Shifu will 
probably win the mage category.</i>

05:42.480 --> 05:45.430
How utterly distasteful.

05:45.430 --> 05:49.220
The winner is one of the 
notorious Rembrandt sisters.

05:49.220 --> 05:53.710
She probably used her wealth to 
acquire expensive magical equipment.

05:54.380 --> 05:56.800
Enough. You disgrace yourselves.

05:56.800 --> 05:59.110
Y-Your Highness...

05:59.580 --> 06:03.120
Their fight was marvelous.

06:03.120 --> 06:05.040
Their desire to try new things

06:05.040 --> 06:08.120
instead of being satisfied with current 
combat techniques is admirable.

06:08.120 --> 06:13.660
But such underhanded fighting is hardly 
suitable for a soldier or knight.

06:13.660 --> 06:16.430
Then what about our nation's hero?

06:16.790 --> 06:22.140
Is it underhanded when he uses his mobility 
to dispatch demons from the skies?

06:22.870 --> 06:25.160
I agree.

06:25.450 --> 06:28.850
Tradition and ceremony don't reduce 
casualties on the battlefield.

06:28.850 --> 06:30.710
They won't protect our lands.

06:31.190 --> 06:34.780
Your words could be taken as 
insults against the hero.

06:35.260 --> 06:37.740
It's distasteful.

06:38.780 --> 06:42.310
I was surprised by their fighting, too.

06:42.310 --> 06:47.730
They would surely fight marvelously 
with the goddess's blessing.

06:48.190 --> 06:51.120
I'm rather looking forward to the next match.

06:52.570 --> 06:58.130
<i>In the second round of the mage category, 
the winner, Shifu, will fight Izumo.</i>

07:00.840 --> 07:02.650
More spirit magic.

07:05.110 --> 07:06.330
Garzloa!

07:12.650 --> 07:14.020
Flamswen.

07:20.450 --> 07:22.960
<i>This is probably over.</i>

07:24.460 --> 07:25.960
<b>Round Two Winner: Shifu</b>

07:27.080 --> 07:30.380
<i>In the second round of the warrior 
category, Jin will fight Daena.</i>

07:36.900 --> 07:39.020
The winner is Jin Rohan.

07:40.120 --> 07:43.440
<i>He's only casting enhancing 
spells between attacks.</i>

07:44.190 --> 07:46.520
<i>His instincts are insane.</i>

07:47.000 --> 07:48.960
<b>Mage Category Final</b>

07:48.940 --> 07:51.130
<i>Shifu's opponent is an older student.</i>

07:51.130 --> 07:55.380
<i>He's apparently good enough to receive 
an offer from the court of Limia.</i>

07:55.380 --> 07:59.300
O goddess, grant me an azure 
yet invisible blade of wind.

08:03.830 --> 08:04.970
Ref?

08:10.740 --> 08:12.820
Az flaga swenia.

08:11.000 --> 08:12.530
Damn it!

08:15.700 --> 08:18.200
The winner is Shifu Rembrandt.

08:19.980 --> 08:21.500
Impressive.

08:21.500 --> 08:26.720
I decided to scare him a little since 
he'll be on Hopleys' team tomorrow.

08:26.720 --> 08:28.440
That was more than a little.

08:28.810 --> 08:31.890
Does this mean you're upset 
about this tournament, too?

08:31.890 --> 08:33.900
I'll leave that up to your imagination.

08:34.840 --> 08:37.170
Jin, I'm sure you know already, but...

08:37.540 --> 08:39.740
Yeah, of course.

08:42.860 --> 08:45.550
Watch me, Kuzunoha-sensei.

08:54.420 --> 08:59.080
It's tradition to wear this to formal events.

08:59.470 --> 09:01.570
I have no complaints.

09:01.570 --> 09:03.110
Let's have a good match.

09:04.500 --> 09:07.980
Your luck ran out when you decided 
to take Kuzunoha's class.

09:09.800 --> 09:16.990
The warrior category final between Ilumgand 
Hopleys and Jin Rohan will now begin!

09:27.370 --> 09:29.520
Noble blood that flows through my body,

09:29.520 --> 09:32.260
awaken to become my blue strength!

09:40.650 --> 09:42.610
R-Ref!

09:44.550 --> 09:48.080
Jin Rohan, you seem to be fighting passively.

09:48.080 --> 09:49.680
Please participate more actively.

09:50.690 --> 09:52.180
Understood.

09:53.890 --> 09:57.510
You bastard! Do you really think 
you'll get away with—

10:18.320 --> 10:22.380
Th-The winner is Jin Rohan.

10:29.070 --> 10:31.230
<i>Yup. Nice work, Jin.</i>

10:31.730 --> 10:36.970
<i>His equipment may be inferior, but his 
level and instincts are way ahead.</i>

10:39.070 --> 10:42.360
This isn't over. There's still the team battle.

10:44.630 --> 10:47.250
I swear... I swear...

10:47.670 --> 10:49.700
I'll kill him.

10:52.270 --> 10:55.680
It's time for the winners of both 
categories to fight each other.

10:56.120 --> 10:58.880
The champion of the whole 
tournament will be decided.

10:59.200 --> 11:03.900
Shifu has a great advantage. 
I'm not sure Jin stands a chance.

11:04.230 --> 11:05.970
None at all.

11:05.970 --> 11:08.980
Jin might have some tricks up his...

11:08.980 --> 11:09.470
Huh?

11:09.840 --> 11:11.210
Forgive me...

11:13.660 --> 11:15.860
but let us end this.

11:23.450 --> 11:26.010
The winner is Shifu Rembrandt.

11:26.490 --> 11:27.830
I am not surprised.

11:27.830 --> 11:29.500
It's the expected outcome

11:29.500 --> 11:30.670
of this tournament.

11:30.670 --> 11:32.110
It's only natural.

11:32.670 --> 11:36.580
<i>The individual event was won 
by the spellcasting beauty,</i>

11:37.360 --> 11:40.050
<i>but the team event would 
take place the following day.</i>

11:40.740 --> 11:44.100
<i>The students' tournament continued.</i>

11:44.950 --> 11:51.170
<i>Meanwhile, Misumi Makoto received 
troubling news from the merchant's guild.</i>

11:53.350 --> 11:57.860
Anyway, they ask that you 
visit the guild tomorrow.

11:58.140 --> 12:01.490
I'm sorry I couldn't do more for you.

12:01.490 --> 12:04.770
<i>Not at all. Don't worry about it.</i>

12:04.770 --> 12:10.750
The dignitaries of every nation have taken 
an interest in the Kuzunoha Trading Company.

12:11.940 --> 12:15.940
Perhaps your day of reckoning has come.

12:19.800 --> 12:21.590
<b>Tournament Team Event Round One</b>

12:20.790 --> 12:21.590
What?

12:21.590 --> 12:23.540
Kuzunoha-sensei can't come?

12:23.540 --> 12:26.880
No. Apparently the merchant's 
guild asked to see him.

12:26.880 --> 12:28.580
Wh-What about Shiki-san?

12:28.580 --> 12:30.760
Shiki-san and his two attendants 
will watch the matches.

12:31.110 --> 12:32.250
Oh, good.

12:32.250 --> 12:33.170
It is?

12:33.170 --> 12:35.230
All you care about is Shiki-san.

12:35.230 --> 12:36.980
M-More importantly,

12:36.980 --> 12:40.100
what changes were made 
to the team event rules?

12:40.560 --> 12:44.790
The party's total level 
must be less than 365.

12:45.560 --> 12:48.530
We'll have to adjust our 
numbers for the match.

12:48.840 --> 12:51.390
So only three of us can fight.

12:51.390 --> 12:52.800
It's ridiculous.

12:53.360 --> 12:56.430
It's not as though that will change anything.

12:56.430 --> 12:57.750
Right?

13:00.260 --> 13:03.950
<i>It's like they're fighting 
scarecrows or wooden dolls.</i>

13:04.980 --> 13:08.490
<i>This Kuzunoha is an incredible teacher.</i>

13:09.490 --> 13:12.140
<i>It would be a shame to allow 
another nation to claim him.</i>

13:12.730 --> 13:15.340
<i>Dangerous, too.</i>

13:16.440 --> 13:19.550
I'm impressed there are students this skilled.

13:19.550 --> 13:21.440
Their teacher's name is Kuzunoha.

13:21.910 --> 13:24.400
He also represents the 
Kuzunoha Trading Company.

13:26.330 --> 13:29.570
There are still great men yet 
to be discovered in this world.

13:30.370 --> 13:35.590
I am Zara Hardis, leader of the 
Rotsgard merchant's guild branch.

13:35.870 --> 13:39.040
<i>My name is Kuzunoha. 
It's an honor to meet you.</i>

13:39.040 --> 13:43.790
An honor? Then why haven't 
you asked to see me until now?

13:44.270 --> 13:48.040
<i>I had to wait a whole month 
for an appointment with you.</i>

13:48.450 --> 13:51.510
<i>Forgive me for not introducing 
myself sooner.</i>

13:52.030 --> 13:54.400
That's a rather delayed apology.

13:54.400 --> 13:57.630
The truth is, I've been asked to investigate

13:57.630 --> 14:01.690
the Kuzunoha Trading Company's 
merchandise and distribution.

14:01.690 --> 14:04.360
Some grave opinions have been 
expressed about your company.

14:04.740 --> 14:06.120
<i>Grave opinions?</i>

14:06.120 --> 14:10.780
That the Kuzunoha Trading Company 
receives help from demons.

14:11.050 --> 14:15.030
<i>I'm offended. We're an honest business.</i>

14:15.030 --> 14:16.750
I'm sure you are.

14:17.030 --> 14:21.720
The temple guaranteed the quality and 
production methods of your products, as well.

14:21.720 --> 14:23.190
<i>The temple?</i>

14:23.190 --> 14:24.470
<i>Oh, that thing the other day.</i>

14:26.070 --> 14:28.560
The issue is with your distribution.

14:28.560 --> 14:30.680
We've confirmed that you purchase

14:30.680 --> 14:34.050
raw materials through markets 
operated directly by the guild.

14:34.050 --> 14:39.720
But we've been unable to confirm any road 
travel records of your carts and wagons.

14:39.720 --> 14:42.350
How are you transporting your materials?

14:42.830 --> 14:44.990
<i>I can't tell him about the demiplane.</i>

14:44.990 --> 14:46.700
<i>I'll have to trick him somehow.</i>

14:47.000 --> 14:50.020
<i>We use the same roads as 
other trading companies,</i>

14:50.020 --> 14:53.420
<i>but because we borrow carts and wagons 
from the Rembrandt Trading Company,</i>

14:53.420 --> 14:56.710
<i>there are no travel records under the 
Kuzunoha Trading Company's name.</i>

14:57.020 --> 14:59.910
I see... But what about this?

15:00.320 --> 15:02.910
These documents compare the materials

15:02.910 --> 15:06.750
you purchased from the market with 
materials used in the products you sell.

15:06.750 --> 15:11.970
It's clear that you're acquiring materials from 
somewhere other than the markets, too.

15:11.970 --> 15:14.460
<i>This is the first I've heard 
of that investigation.</i>

15:14.460 --> 15:17.520
<i>If you'd told me about it, 
I could've offered my cooperation.</i>

15:17.520 --> 15:18.880
Your cooperation?

15:18.880 --> 15:22.570
It's for the guild to decide if your 
trading company is innocent or not.

15:22.840 --> 15:27.290
<i>Is it not natural for me to cooperate with 
your investigation and clear my name?</i>

15:27.980 --> 15:29.500
You are naïve.

15:29.850 --> 15:32.980
I'm amazed you can operate 
a trading company like that.

15:32.980 --> 15:36.720
Why can't you behave appropriately 
for your status and circumstances?

15:36.720 --> 15:37.410
<i>Why?</i>

15:38.090 --> 15:40.700
<i>What did I do to deserve this?</i>

15:41.990 --> 15:43.810
<i>Allow me to be direct.</i>

15:43.810 --> 15:46.370
<i>What is it that you want me to do?</i>

15:47.840 --> 15:53.790
We want you to submit your distribution 
methods to the guild and share them with us.

15:54.090 --> 15:58.760
<i>Is he trying to extort me by offering 
conditions I can't accept?</i>

15:59.200 --> 16:01.410
<i>I can't agree to those terms.</i>

16:01.410 --> 16:03.980
<i>Is this something we can 
resolve with money?</i>

16:03.980 --> 16:07.440
You're really not cut out 
to be a merchant, are you?

16:08.670 --> 16:13.360
You just admitted to the existence of a 
transportation method you're hiding from us.

16:13.360 --> 16:17.330
That lie has damaged our trust in you.

16:17.590 --> 16:21.280
A decent merchant would never 
do anything like that.

16:22.160 --> 16:25.630
Then you asked if this matter 
could be resolved with money.

16:25.630 --> 16:27.870
That was an unbelievably bad move, as well.

16:27.870 --> 16:29.710
Do you have any idea of the scale

16:29.710 --> 16:32.600
of the trading companies that have 
submitted complaints against you?

16:32.860 --> 16:34.560
<i>I-I...</i>

16:34.560 --> 16:40.020
Since Rembrandt got involved, 
I expected more from you.

16:40.020 --> 16:43.340
But your judgment and comprehension 
are utterly lacking.

16:43.340 --> 16:47.220
You're an incompetent child 
who's made it on luck alone.

16:48.780 --> 16:52.230
For now, you will pay us 90% 
of your monthly profits.

16:52.230 --> 16:54.700
Then no one will have 
anything to complain about.

16:55.160 --> 16:56.650
<i>Ninety percent of my profits?</i>

16:56.960 --> 17:02.630
These companies earn dozens, if not hundreds 
of times as much as yours annually.

17:02.630 --> 17:05.580
They're not going to ask 
for just a few gold coins.

17:05.870 --> 17:08.520
<i>Th-That's a clearly unreasonable demand.</i>

17:08.520 --> 17:10.780
<i>Are you going to allow this extortion?</i>

17:10.780 --> 17:13.360
You said you would pay.

17:13.360 --> 17:15.720
It's not the guild's concern.

17:15.720 --> 17:18.030
<i>The nail that sticks out gets 
hammered down, does it?</i>

17:18.030 --> 17:20.980
<i>I see it doesn't pay to be 
an honest businessman.</i>

17:21.280 --> 17:23.490
There's no end to your naïveté.

17:23.490 --> 17:26.300
Your stores employ mostly 
demihumans, don't they?

17:26.300 --> 17:30.150
Then why not sell to only demihumans, too?

17:30.150 --> 17:34.530
If you set up stalls outside cities, 
you'd be unrestricted.

17:34.530 --> 17:35.720
<i>This asshole...</i>

17:35.720 --> 17:41.000
Those who wish to become merchants must 
knock on the doors built by their predecessors,

17:41.000 --> 17:43.610
learn the basics of business, 
and build relationships.

17:43.610 --> 17:45.950
Only then can they open their own shops!

17:45.950 --> 17:50.040
No one's allowed to conduct business 
just because they have the funds.

17:52.080 --> 17:55.910
Oh, and it doesn't matter how 
strong your followers are.

17:55.910 --> 17:58.330
If you attempt to resolve this with violence,

17:58.330 --> 18:01.360
the Kuzunoha Trading Company will instantly 
be branded allies of the demons.

18:01.360 --> 18:03.740
You'll be traitors to hyumankind.

18:03.740 --> 18:04.600
<i>This is ridiculous.</i>

18:04.600 --> 18:07.570
No. You're just naïve.

18:08.010 --> 18:11.500
Regarding the money, 
the guild will intervene,

18:11.500 --> 18:14.510
so close down your shop 
and go back to Tsige.

18:15.070 --> 18:19.600
This is what you get for not doing what 
you were supposed to do, Kuzunoha.

18:19.600 --> 18:22.910
Is your idea of being an honest 
businessman bumming around?

18:22.910 --> 18:26.360
By my values, I'd call that being lazy.

18:27.100 --> 18:31.090
<i>You're being rather kind 
for someone mocking me.</i>

18:31.090 --> 18:35.050
Because then Rembrandt will owe me a favor.

18:36.250 --> 18:40.350
He must be getting old to 
show this kind of weakness.

18:40.740 --> 18:44.650
<i>Am I causing problems 
for Rembrandt-san, too?</i>

18:48.730 --> 18:52.970
But you will tell us about 
your distribution methods.

18:52.970 --> 18:55.140
Now talk.

18:56.380 --> 19:01.120
<i>I didn't know what to do anymore,</i>

19:01.120 --> 19:07.600
<i>so I explained that I used my magically 
powerful follower's teleportation spell.</i>

19:08.450 --> 19:10.410
<i>Naturally, I didn't mention the demiplane.</i>

19:11.520 --> 19:15.500
<i>I thought my business had been going well.</i>

19:17.330 --> 19:21.050
Very well. I'll deal with that 
representative this very instant.

19:21.050 --> 19:22.880
Mio, calm down.

19:22.880 --> 19:25.260
We should've gone with you.

19:25.640 --> 19:30.540
If we'd gone with him, 
it might've turned into a bloodbath.

19:30.540 --> 19:33.050
Don't let it bother you, Young Master.

19:33.430 --> 19:38.050
The master became a merchant so he 
could provide everyone with medicine.

19:38.050 --> 19:42.820
Why does he need to know how to get along 
with merchants who only care about profits?

19:42.820 --> 19:44.700
You're being naïve.

19:44.700 --> 19:49.170
I won't say he did the wrong thing, 
but this is part of doing business.

19:49.450 --> 19:52.640
Especially if you're 
conducting honest business.

19:53.120 --> 19:55.590
There's something wrong with both of you!

19:55.590 --> 19:59.960
Young Master, this could be an 
opportunity to abandon hyumankind.

19:59.960 --> 20:03.600
Don't you intend to establish a 
relationship with demons eventually anyway?

20:03.600 --> 20:08.300
Demons are more tolerant of other 
species than hyumans, too.

20:08.300 --> 20:12.140
This is all too complicated for me,

20:12.140 --> 20:18.570
but I don't think he needs to serve anyone 
who would exploit his pure benevolence!

20:19.260 --> 20:22.310
Yeah. Tomoe is right.

20:22.310 --> 20:24.540
I intend to establish a 
relationship with demons.

20:25.020 --> 20:30.780
Once the academy festival is over, I plan 
to borrow or acquire the land Tomoe found.

20:31.350 --> 20:34.740
I may end up owing the demons a lot.

20:35.210 --> 20:39.000
Ideally, I'd like to continue 
doing business with hyumans

20:39.000 --> 20:43.010
while maintaining a connection 
with demons, but...

20:53.270 --> 20:56.350
Kaleneon, once part of Elysion.

20:56.730 --> 21:00.530
This was my parents' home country.

21:01.150 --> 21:06.980
My parents met here, became adventurers, 
and traveled around the world.

21:07.220 --> 21:10.440
In other words, it's like my home country, too.

21:10.440 --> 21:13.900
Aren't Eva the librarian and 
Luria of Gotetsu from there?

21:14.200 --> 21:16.840
Yes. It's their homeland, too.

21:16.840 --> 21:20.890
That's why I'm going to ask 
them to make a decision.

21:21.270 --> 21:23.910
If they agree...

21:29.010 --> 21:30.670
That sounds interesting!

21:30.670 --> 21:36.150
Indeed. It could be the trump card 
that solves your current problems.

21:36.510 --> 21:40.350
I have no complaints with your decision.

21:41.020 --> 21:43.320
<i>They all accepted my choice,</i>

21:44.480 --> 21:46.270
<i>so I won't hesitate anymore.</i>

21:49.080 --> 21:51.910
<i>The two heroes sided with the hyumans,</i>

21:52.560 --> 21:56.900
<i>so there should be no problem with 
the third man from another world</i>

21:56.900 --> 21:59.200
<i>overlooking some of the demons' actions.</i>

21:59.720 --> 22:02.760
<i>Right, shitty goddess?</i>

23:34.920 --> 23:39.220
<i>Night Sixteen: "A Certain Student's Secret."</i>

23:35.220 --> 23:39.930
<b>Next Time</b>

23:36.340 --> 23:39.930
<b>A Certain Student's Secret</b>
